        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I've finally found time to try and see what this can be caused by.\r\n\r\nAs far as I can tell, 'mini.completion' works as expected in every case here (after `foo.`, after `foo.p`, after `std::`):\r\n- It sends proper 'textDocument/completion' request with proper context.\r\n- It receives the result `{ isIncomplete = true, items = {} }`, meaning that LSP server says there are no completion candidates.\r\n\r\nFor what it is worth, I can observe the same behavior with 'hrsh7th/nvim-cmp' and 'hrsh7th/cmp-nvim-lsp' source. So I don't think it is a problem on 'mini.completion' side. I tried searching issues for this in 'rust-lang/rust-analyzer', but was not successful.\r\n\r\nClosing as this looks like an upstream problem. If you'll have more details, feel free to post a comment here and we'll try to take a further look.",
